  "result": "I've completed the overdue report feature with all 283 tests passing. The implementation:\n\n**src/reports.js (new):**\n- `overdueInvoices(invoices, asOf)` function that returns invoices with status 'issued' or 'partially_paid' where dueDate < asOf\n- Returns array of `{ number, customerId, dueDate, daysOverdue, due }` sorted by most overdue first\n- Calculates daysOverdue as the difference between asOf and dueDate\n- Uses balanceDue() for accurate remaining amounts accounting for payments\n\n**test/reports.test.js (new):**\n- 25 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Empty/no-overdue cases\n  - Single and multiple overdue invoices\n  - Correct sorting (most overdue first)\n  - All required fields (number, customerId, dueDate, daysOverdue, due)\n  - Filtering (excludes draft, paid, not-yet-due invoices)\n  - Edge cases (daysOverdue=1, large daysOverdue, mixed customers)\n  - Various payment terms (NET14, NET30, EOM)\n  - Multiple payments on single invoice\n  - Large invoice volumes\n\nReady to commit when you approve.",
